{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:01:00.480Z","tool_name":"update_topic","tool_id":"update_topic__call_386488","parameters":{"summary":"Computational exploration for K=2 through 15 revealed a striking pattern: a stable set exists if and only if K is even, and when K=2m is even, the unique stable set is {(0, m, m), (m, 0, m), (m, m, 0)}. I will now verify why this holds mathematically and construct a complete proof for all K >= 2.","title":"Developing the Mathematical Proof","strategic_intent":"Develop the mathematical proof characterizing all stable sets for all K >= 2."}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:01:06.167Z","tool_name":"write_file","tool_id":"write_file__call_386521","parameters":{"file_path":"/work/verify_simple.py","content":"# Let's double check K=2..7 with a completely independent, minimal-pruning backtracking search\nfrom explore import dominates\n\ndef verify_simple(K):\n    pts = [(a, b, K - a - b) for a in range(K + 1) for b in range(K + 1 - a)]\n    n = len(pts)\n    adj = [0] * n\n    dom_by = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if dominates(pts[i], pts[j]):\n                adj[i] |= (1 << j) | (1 << i)\n                adj[j] |= (1 << i) | (1 << j)\n                dom_by[j] |= (1 << i)\n            elif i == j:\n                adj[i] |= (1 << i)\n    \n    # Independent set S (bitmask) such that for all j not in S, S & dom_by[j] != 0\n    sols = []\n    def rec(idx, S, forbidden):\n        # check if any already-passed or future vertex cannot be dominated\n        for j in range(n):\n            if not (S & (1 << j)) and not (dom_by[j] & S):\n                # can j still be put in S or dominated by something >= idx not in forbidden?\n                rem = ((1 << n) - (1 << idx)) & ~forbidden\n                if not ((j >= idx and not (forbidden & (1 << j))) or (dom_by[j] & rem)):\n                    return\n        if idx == n:\n            sols.append([pts[i] for i in range(n) if S & (1 << i)])\n            return\n        # branch: put idx in S (if not forbidden)\n        if not (forbidden & (1 << idx)):\n            rec(idx + 1, S | (1 << idx), forbidden | adj[idx])\n        # branch: do not put idx in S\n        rec(idx + 1, S, forbidden)\n\n    rec(0, 0, 0)\n    print(f\"K={K}: {len(sols)} sols:\", sols)\n\nfor K in range(2, 8):\n    verify_simple(K)\n"}}
