{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:08:37.407Z","tool_id":"update_topic__call_421037","status":"success","output":"## 📂 Topic: **Completed Solution and Submission**\n\n**Summary:**\nI have completed the investigation, computational verification, and mathematical proofs for the grid majority division stable sets problem. We proved that a stable set exists if and only if K >= 2 is even, and that for every even K = 2m, the unique stable set is {(m, m, 0), (m, 0, m), (0, m, m)}. The complete answers and proofs have been written and verified in /work/answer.md, and I am now writing /work/SUBMIT to conclude the task.\n\n> [!STRATEGY]\n> **Intent:** Recap the completed work and write /work/SUBMIT to finalize the submission."}
